%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0bed9661326f77c4c8582962c4420e24, type: 3}
  m_Name: TutorialDataSO
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TutorialDataSO
  tutorialName: 'Tutorial Start '
  tutorialDialogueDatas:
  - characterName: Dr.Kirana
    characterSprite: {fileID: -1687011945, guid: 56cf509b78d164741a5ad60c05a60ab8, type: 3}
    tutorialDialogueLine: Before we begin, I'll show you how our Passive Acoustic
      Monitoring, or PAM, system works.
    listHighligthId: []
    tutorialMission: 0
  - characterName: Dr.Kirana
    characterSprite: {fileID: -1687011945, guid: 56cf509b78d164741a5ad60c05a60ab8, type: 3}
    tutorialDialogueLine: Instead of watching the forest with cameras, we listen
      to it. Every sound tells us something about the condition of the ecosystem.
    listHighligthId: []
    tutorialMission: 0
  - characterName: Dr.Kirana
    characterSprite: {fileID: -1687011945, guid: 56cf509b78d164741a5ad60c05a60ab8, type: 3}
    tutorialDialogueLine: This is the Bioacoustic Monitoring screen. It displays
      the PAM Device deployed throughout the forest.
    listHighligthId: []
    tutorialMission: 0
  - characterName: Dr.Kirana
    characterSprite: {fileID: -1687011945, guid: 56cf509b78d164741a5ad60c05a60ab8, type: 3}
    tutorialDialogueLine: On the right is your <color=red> Task Board </color>.
    listHighligthId:
    - TaskMonitor
    tutorialMission: 0
  - characterName: Dr.Kirana
    characterSprite: {fileID: -1687011945, guid: 56cf509b78d164741a5ad60c05a60ab8, type: 3}
    tutorialDialogueLine: Each assignment includes an audio clue. Click the <color=red>
      speaker icon </color> whenever you need to hear the reference sound again.
    listHighligthId:
    - TaskMonitor
    tutorialMission: 0
  - characterName: Dr.Kirana
    characterSprite: {fileID: -1687011945, guid: 56cf509b78d164741a5ad60c05a60ab8, type: 3}
    tutorialDialogueLine: Your job is to match what you hear from the forest with
      the correct task.
    listHighligthId:
    - TaskMonitor
    tutorialMission: 0
  - characterName: Dr.Kirana
    characterSprite: {fileID: -1687011945, guid: 56cf509b78d164741a5ad60c05a60ab8, type: 3}
    tutorialDialogueLine: At the bottom right is the <color=red> Forest Health Indicator</color>.
    listHighligthId:
    - ForestMonitor
    tutorialMission: 0
  - characterName: Dr.Kirana
    characterSprite: {fileID: -1687011945, guid: 56cf509b78d164741a5ad60c05a60ab8, type: 3}
    tutorialDialogueLine: Bird Icon is <color=red>BiodiversityIndicator</color>,
      it reflects the variety of wildlife we've successfully identified.
    listHighligthId:
    - ForestMonitor
    tutorialMission: 0
  - characterName: Dr.Kirana
    characterSprite: {fileID: -1687011945, guid: 56cf509b78d164741a5ad60c05a60ab8, type: 3}
    tutorialDialogueLine: Warning Icon is <color=red> Threat Level </color>, it represents
      disturbances such as illegal logging or poaching detected in the area.
    listHighligthId:
    - ForestMonitor
    tutorialMission: 0
  - characterName: Dr.Kirana
    characterSprite: {fileID: -1687011945, guid: 56cf509b78d164741a5ad60c05a60ab8, type: 3}
    tutorialDialogueLine: Tree Icon is <color=red> Forest Sustainability </color>,
      it influenced by both biodiversity and forest threats
    listHighligthId:
    - ForestMonitor
    tutorialMission: 0
  - characterName: Dr.Kirana
    characterSprite: {fileID: -1687011945, guid: 56cf509b78d164741a5ad60c05a60ab8, type: 3}
    tutorialDialogueLine: Every correct decision helps keep the forest healthy.
    listHighligthId:
    - ForestMonitor
    tutorialMission: 0
  tutorialDialoguePosition: 0
